---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const manifestUrl = "https://xtreemze.github.io/slipmat-companion/manifest.json";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Set up Slipmat Companion"
  description="Guided installation and verification for the Slipmat Companion Audio Gateway Jellyfin plugin."
>
  <section class="section" style="border-top:0; padding-top:clamp(3rem,8vw,6rem)">
    <p class="eyebrow">Guided setup</p>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.7rem,7vw,5.6rem)">Connect Companion.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Complete the required Jellyfin installation first. Cloud projection and provider credentials are optional and should only be configured when you need those modules.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="required-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="required-title">Required</h2>
      <p>Your progress is stored only in this browser. These controls do not configure Jellyfin or send data anywhere.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="steps" data-checklist>
      <div class="step">
        <input id="step-repository" type="checkbox" data-step="repository" />
        <div>
          <label for="step-repository"><h2>1. Add the plugin repository</h2></label>
          <p>In Jellyfin, open <strong>Dashboard → Plugins → Repositories</strong> and add:</p>
          <div class="install-command">
            <code>{manifestUrl}</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy={manifestUrl}>Copy</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <input id="step-install" type="checkbox" data-step="install" />
        <div>
          <label for="step-install"><h2>2. Install Audio Gateway</h2></label>
          <p>Open the Jellyfin plugin catalog, install <strong>Audio Gateway</strong>, then restart Jellyfin so the plugin can register its native services and dashboard page.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <input id="step-verify" type="checkbox" data-step="verify" />
        <div>
          <label for="step-verify"><h2>3. Verify capabilities</h2></label>
          <p>Open the Audio Gateway dashboard in Jellyfin. Core batching and integrated analysis should work without an external analyzer. Missing optional modules are ordinary fallback conditions.</p>
          <p>For protocol-level verification, the plugin exposes <code>/Plugins/AudioGateway/diagnostics/capabilities</code>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="optional-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="optional-title">Optional modules</h2>
      <p>Enable only the capabilities you intend to use. These remain adapters and accelerators, not new canonical state owners.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="number">PODCASTS</span>
        <h3>Podcast Index search</h3>
        <p>Configure Podcast Index API credentials as Jellyfin host environment variables. Secrets stay server-side and are never emitted to browser clients.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="number">CLOUD</span>
        <h3>Read-only rclone VFS</h3>
        <p>Install and configure rclone on the Jellyfin host, then create bounded VFS profiles in the plugin dashboard. Companion does not expose rclone RC.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="number">ADVANCED</span>
        <h3>Artifact store override</h3>
        <p>The plugin provisions its own writable store by default. Override it only for deployments that intentionally manage a dedicated location.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="note">
      Cloud-mounted media is excluded from automatic Companion analysis traversal. Missing cloud analysis remains request-driven so a scheduled background pass cannot materialize an entire remote library.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2>Continue in Slipmat.</h2>
      <p>Once Jellyfin reports the extension as healthy, Slipmat can negotiate the optional modules it understands. No separate Companion login or second media library is required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/xtreemze/slipmat-companion#active-endpoints">Read technical reference</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="../">Back to overview</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    const storageKey = "slipmat-companion-onboarding-v1";
    const checks = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>("[data-step]"));

    try {
      const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey) ?? "{}");
      checks.forEach((check) => {
        check.checked = Boolean(saved[check.dataset.step ?? ""]);
      });
    } catch {
      localStorage.removeItem(storageKey);
    }

    checks.forEach((check) => {
      check.addEventListener("change", () => {
        const state = Object.fromEntries(
          checks.map((item) => [item.dataset.step, item.checked]),
        );
        localStorage.setItem(storageKey, JSON.stringify(state));
      });
    });

    document.querySelectorAll("[data-copy]").forEach((element) => {
      const button = element as HTMLButtonElement;
      button.addEventListener("click", async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        const value = button.getAttribute("data-copy");
        if (!value) return;
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(value);
        button.textContent = "Copied";
      });
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
